  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="angriterion-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">אנקריטיריון</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾnqryṭyrywn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">anqriṭerion</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="angriterion-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>decision of examining tribunal</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>ἀνακριτηριον</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>אמר ר' יהודה בר' סימון בשר ודם תולין לו 
                     <app>
                        <lem>אנקליטון</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1 V">אנקלימון</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox2">אנקליטין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#K">סנקליטון</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1">אנקריטיריון</rdg>
                     </app> מדוכס לאיפרכוס מאיפרכוס לאיסטרטלטיס ואת בשביל שאין לך מי יתלה לך 
                     <app>
                        <lem>אנקליטון</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K V">אנקליטין</rdg>
                     </app> לא תעשה משפט</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">49,9</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">II 510: 4</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">אנקליטון</ref>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">דוכס</ref>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">איפרכוס</ref>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">איסטרטלטיס</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>R. Yehuda be-R. Simon said: (Abraham pleaded thus:) ‘Even in the case of a human judge, an anqriṭerion can be made from the commander to the prefect and from the prefect to the governor; but you, because no appeal can be made from your judgment, will you not do justly? (cf. Freedman / Simon I 429)</quote>
                  </cit>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>An independent reading of Vat 1 for <bibl type="ancient">GenR 49,9</bibl>; attested only there. For further literature cf. Sperber. Cf. <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">אנקליטון</ref>, <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">אנקלימון</ref></note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Sperber (1984)</title>
                  <citedRange>50</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
